  triage:title "doc-named herdr_queue_ephemeral.rs test file missing; 8 of 9 in-scope tests relocated, 1 genuinely absent" ;
  triage:description "quality-mgr QA-1 (quality-mgr, rust-qa-agent, req-qa), PR #1407 @ b617a9eab, https://github.com/randlee/atm-core/pull/1407#issuecomment-5642789392. The doc-named new file crates/atm-http-runtime/tests/herdr_queue_ephemeral.rs does not exist anywhere in the export. req-qa's more granular check corrects the initial ground-truth note: 8 of the 9 in-scope runtime tests actually exist, verbatim by name, relocated into the pre-existing unit-test modules of herdr_queue_wake.rs and storage_and_nudge_router.rs. Exactly one in-scope named test, blocked_member_with_open_item_escalates_not_reminded, does not exist anywhere under any name. fenix's ruling (https://github.com/randlee/atm-core/pull/1407#issuecomment-5642806916): STANDS -- write blocked_member_with_open_item_escalates_not_reminded; the 8 relocated tests move into the doc-named file via #[cfg(test)] #[path = \"../../tests/herdr_queue_ephemeral.rs\"] under herdr_queue_wake's tests, with autotests = false set in Cargo.toml; no sprint-doc amendment." ;
